From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: the digital internal mic wins a tie

On laptops whose microphone is digital (AMD's ACP, Intel's SOF DMIC), the
HD-Audio codec often reports an internal mic as well that nothing is wired
to. CRAS lists both as INTERNAL_MIC, with the same priority and plugged
time, and Chrome chose the codec's: every app, Chrome's and Linux apps',
recorded silence until the user picked the other one by hand (Dell
laptop: "HD-Audio Generic: Realtek codec Analog" peaked at 30 of 32767,
"acp" recorded room noise at RMS ~350).

LessBuiltInPriority() now puts an internal mic on a digital mic controller
(device name starting "acp", or containing "dmic") above another internal
mic of the same priority. A user's own choice still wins (user priority).

diff --git a/chromeos/ash/components/audio/audio_device.cc b/chromeos/ash/components/audio/audio_device.cc
index 06329e7b86286..42cb7adef2f8e 100644
--- a/chromeos/ash/components/audio/audio_device.cc
+++ b/chromeos/ash/components/audio/audio_device.cc
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include "ash/constants/ash_features.h"
 #include "base/format_macros.h"
 #include "base/strings/string_number_conversions.h"
+#include "base/strings/string_util.h"
 #include "base/strings/stringprintf.h"
 #include "base/strings/utf_string_conversions.h"
 
@@ -220,11 +221,27 @@ bool AudioDevice::IsInternalSpeaker() const {
   return type == AudioDeviceType::kInternalSpeaker;
 }
 
+// NickelOS: an internal mic on a digital mic controller (AMD's ACP, Intel's
+// SOF DMIC). On laptops whose microphone is digital, the HD-Audio codec often
+// reports an internal mic too that nothing is wired to; CRAS lists both with
+// the same priority and the same plugged time, and Chrome chose the codec's,
+// so every app recorded silence (Dell laptop, 2026-10-23).
+static bool IsDigitalInternalMic(const AudioDevice& device) {
+  if (device.type != AudioDeviceType::kInternalMic) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  const std::string name = base::ToLowerASCII(device.device_name);
+  return name.starts_with("acp") || name.find("dmic") != std::string::npos;
+}
+
 bool LessBuiltInPriority(const AudioDevice& a, const AudioDevice& b) {
   if (a.priority < b.priority) {
     return true;
   } else if (b.priority < a.priority) {
     return false;
+  } else if (IsDigitalInternalMic(a) != IsDigitalInternalMic(b)) {
+    // NickelOS: the digital internal mic wins a tie.
+    return IsDigitalInternalMic(b);
   } else if (a.plugged_time < b.plugged_time) {
     return true;
   } else {
